.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# ── Notebook noise ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Generated artifacts. Regenerated by the verify tier. The published benchmark table
# travels with a tagged revision rather than an archive deposit, and the checksums that
# make the tag verifiable are the one exception re-included below.
artifacts/*

# Kept for its source and its reference list; its build products and the IEEE
# class files are not ours and regenerate from a compile.
docs/prior/latex/**/*.aux
docs/prior/latex/**/*.log
docs/prior/latex/**/*.out
docs/prior/latex/**/*.bbl
docs/prior/latex/**/*.blg
docs/prior/latex/**/*.synctex.gz
docs/prior/latex/**/*.pfb
docs/prior/latex/**/*.tfm
docs/prior/latex/**/*.cls
docs/prior/latex/**/*.bst
docs/prior/latex/**/*.sty

# The authors' photographs. IEEE Access prints a biography with a portrait;
# Neurocomputing does not, and this repository is published as a tagged release.
# A personal photograph of four named people is not something to publish as a
# side effect of keeping a manuscript's sources.
docs/prior/latex/**/ISM.jpeg
docs/prior/latex/**/MPR.jpeg
docs/prior/latex/**/MPR.png
docs/prior/latex/**/S_sarmiento.jpg
docs/prior/latex/**/VASHphoto.jpeg
docs/prior/latex/**/*.map
docs/prior/latex/**/*.fd
# IEEE's own branding, shipped with its template. Not ours to redistribute.
docs/prior/latex/**/logo.png
docs/prior/latex/**/notaglinelogo.png
docs/prior/latex/**/bullet.png

# The artifacts the paper cites, which are the results this repository exists to carry.
# Everything else under artifacts/ is regenerable intermediate output and stays out: the
# tokenised corpus cache alone is 8.3 GB. The parent is written as `artifacts/*` rather
# than `artifacts/` because git does not descend into a directory ignored with a trailing
# slash, and a negation inside one has no effect — which is also why each parent below is
# re-included before the file inside it, a step the first attempt left out and which cost
# every single-file path its place.
#
# These were untracked until it was noticed that the data availability statement promised
# them and the checksum manifest described them, while a clone contained neither.
!artifacts/benchmark/
!artifacts/benchmark/table.csv
!artifacts/benchmark/summary.json
!artifacts/space/
!artifacts/space/enumeration.csv
!artifacts/space/enumeration_summary.json
!artifacts/characterisation/
!artifacts/characterisation/**
!artifacts/surrogate/
!artifacts/surrogate/**
!artifacts/search/
!artifacts/search/**
!artifacts/sampling/
!artifacts/sampling/**
!artifacts/transfer/
!artifacts/transfer/analysis.json
!artifacts/battery/
!artifacts/battery/analysis.json
!artifacts/references/
!artifacts/references/verification.json
!artifacts/audit/
!artifacts/audit/prior_protocol.json
!artifacts/campaign/
!artifacts/campaign/cost.json
!artifacts/campaign/progress.json
!artifacts/manifests/
!artifacts/manifests/runs.jsonl
!artifacts/replication/
!artifacts/replication/manifest.json
!artifacts/image/
!artifacts/image/published.json
!artifacts/release/
!artifacts/release/checksums.txt

# The built Overleaf project. Regenerated in place by `cli overleaf`, so tracking it
# churns the history with every rebuild and duplicates whatever the latest snapshot in
# docs/manuscript/versions already holds. The snapshots are the versions worth keeping;
# this folder is the working copy.
submission-neurocomputing/

# ── Not in this repository ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This repository holds the code and the experiments. Two things that drove the
# rebuild stay on the authors' machines instead.
#
# The referee reports on the earlier submission: third-party writing addressed to
# an editor, used here to decide what to fix and not ours to publish. The
# objection registry quotes them and checks every quote against them, and reports
# its own inability to do so where they are absent.
docs/reviews/
#
# The earlier article, its thesis and its LaTeX project. They belong to a
# different paper. What this one needed from them — the reference list and the
# audit's figures — is frozen as source: docs/manuscript/references.bib and
# artifacts/audit/prior_protocol.json.
docs/prior/
#
# The manuscript itself, its reference list and the numbered versions of it. The
# paper lives with its authors and in Overleaf; this repository holds what
# produced the numbers in it. `cli overleaf` builds the project from a local
# checkout that has them and says so plainly when it does not.
docs/manuscript/
#
# Planning documents and assistant configuration. The change proposals, the design
# notes and the task list record what was intended and in what order; this repository
# carries what was implemented and what it measured. The objection registry cites the
# task list for objections that have no artifact yet, and reports those citations as
# kept locally rather than counting them broken.
openspec/
.claude/
docs/environment.md
#
# Generated documents that belong to the paper rather than to the pipeline. Both are
# regenerated by a command — `cli replication` and `cli manuscript` — from the code and
# the artifacts that are tracked here, so what they describe is in the repository even
# when they are not.
# docs/REPLICATION.md — published here: the README sends the reader to it
# docs/TABLES.md — published here for the same reason
